Restore the positional-only parameter syntax to fissix's grammar.

fissix forked lib2to3 from CPython at 3.9.0a5 and its Grammar.txt predates
the change that taught the lib2to3 parser PEP 570.  The two productions for
parameter lists therefore have no place for the '/' separator, and any
source that uses one -- which by now is most of the Python 3 standard
library -- fails to parse with

    ParseError: bad input: type=17, value='/'

where Apple's 2to3, running CPython 3.9's lib2to3, reads it fine.  2to3 is
for Python 2 source, which never had positional-only parameters, but it is
routinely pointed at a mixed tree, and a tool that stops on a file Apple's
converts is not a drop-in replacement for it.

The two productions here are CPython's own, from Lib/lib2to3/Grammar.txt as
of 3.9 (PSF License 2.0), which is what fissix is a fork of and what Apple
ship.  With them applied the file is identical to CPython's; nothing else
in the grammar had drifted.

Applied to the installed copy by mk/scripts/install-2to3.sh.  The submodule
itself is not touched.

--- a/fissix/Grammar.txt	2026-09-07 03:02:42
+++ b/fissix/Grammar.txt	2026-09-07 03:02:42
@@ -18,15 +18,55 @@
 async_funcdef: ASYNC funcdef
 funcdef: 'def' NAME parameters ['->' test] ':' suite
 parameters: '(' [typedargslist] ')'
-typedargslist: ((tfpdef ['=' test] ',')*
-                ('*' [tname] (',' tname ['=' test])* [',' ['**' tname [',']]] | '**' tname [','])
-                | tfpdef ['=' test] (',' tfpdef ['=' test])* [','])
+
+# The following definition for typedarglist is equivalent to this set of rules:
+#
+#     arguments = argument (',' argument)*
+#     argument = tfpdef ['=' test]
+#     kwargs = '**' tname [',']
+#     args = '*' [tname]
+#     kwonly_kwargs = (',' argument)* [',' [kwargs]]
+#     args_kwonly_kwargs = args kwonly_kwargs | kwargs
+#     poskeyword_args_kwonly_kwargs = arguments [',' [args_kwonly_kwargs]]
+#     typedargslist_no_posonly  = poskeyword_args_kwonly_kwargs | args_kwonly_kwargs
+#     typedarglist = arguments ',' '/' [',' [typedargslist_no_posonly]])|(typedargslist_no_posonly)"
+#
+# It needs to be fully expanded to allow our LL(1) parser to work on it.
+
+typedargslist: tfpdef ['=' test] (',' tfpdef ['=' test])* ',' '/' [
+                     ',' [((tfpdef ['=' test] ',')* ('*' [tname] (',' tname ['=' test])*
+                            [',' ['**' tname [',']]] | '**' tname [','])
+                     | tfpdef ['=' test] (',' tfpdef ['=' test])* [','])]
+                ] | ((tfpdef ['=' test] ',')* ('*' [tname] (',' tname ['=' test])*
+                     [',' ['**' tname [',']]] | '**' tname [','])
+                     | tfpdef ['=' test] (',' tfpdef ['=' test])* [','])
+
 tname: NAME [':' test]
 tfpdef: tname | '(' tfplist ')'
 tfplist: tfpdef (',' tfpdef)* [',']
-varargslist: ((vfpdef ['=' test] ',')*
-              ('*' [vname] (',' vname ['=' test])*  [',' ['**' vname [',']]] | '**' vname [','])
-              | vfpdef ['=' test] (',' vfpdef ['=' test])* [','])
+
+# The following definition for varargslist is equivalent to this set of rules:
+#
+#     arguments = argument (',' argument )*
+#     argument = vfpdef ['=' test]
+#     kwargs = '**' vname [',']
+#     args = '*' [vname]
+#     kwonly_kwargs = (',' argument )* [',' [kwargs]]
+#     args_kwonly_kwargs = args kwonly_kwargs | kwargs
+#     poskeyword_args_kwonly_kwargs = arguments [',' [args_kwonly_kwargs]]
+#     vararglist_no_posonly = poskeyword_args_kwonly_kwargs | args_kwonly_kwargs
+#     varargslist = arguments ',' '/' [','[(vararglist_no_posonly)]] | (vararglist_no_posonly)
+#
+# It needs to be fully expanded to allow our LL(1) parser to work on it.
+
+varargslist: vfpdef ['=' test ](',' vfpdef ['=' test])* ',' '/' [',' [
+                     ((vfpdef ['=' test] ',')* ('*' [vname] (',' vname ['=' test])*
+                            [',' ['**' vname [',']]] | '**' vname [','])
+                            | vfpdef ['=' test] (',' vfpdef ['=' test])* [','])
+                     ]] | ((vfpdef ['=' test] ',')*
+                     ('*' [vname] (',' vname ['=' test])*  [',' ['**' vname [',']]]| '**' vname [','])
+                     | vfpdef ['=' test] (',' vfpdef ['=' test])* [','])
+
 vname: NAME
 vfpdef: vname | '(' vfplist ')'
 vfplist: vfpdef (',' vfpdef)* [',']
